@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<article class="col-lg-9">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated @DateTime.Now.ToString("MMMM yyyy")</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you register, we store your full name, email address and a securely hashed password — never the password itself. As you use the site we record your enrolments, quiz attempts and discussion posts so your progress can be shown back to you on the My Learning page.</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">How we use it</h2>
    <p>Your data is used only to run your account: logging you in, tracking which courses you have joined, and showing your quiz history. We do not sell or share it with third parties.</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Cookies</h2>
    <p>PadhaiHub uses a single login cookie to keep you signed in. It does not track you across other websites.</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can leave any course from the My Learning page, edit your profile at any time, or email us to request your account be removed.</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:support@padhaihub.com">support@padhaihub.com</a>.</p>
</article>